# Elite Trade FX conventions

Stack is Vite + React + TypeScript + Redux Toolkit + React Router + Tailwind v4.
Do not introduce Next.js, Prisma, or a second state library unless the user asks.

## Folders

- `src/pages` — thin route files. They render one container.
- `src/containers` — screen UI, grouped by Landing, Auth, Portal, Admin.
- `src/components` — shared layout and UI (Marketing, Portal, Admin, Auth, `_common`).
- `src/router` — `createBrowserRouter`, `AllRoutes`, public/private guards.
- `src/store` — slices in `store/slices`, API-style thunks later in `store/actions`.
- `src/data` — static design content until a backend exists.
- `src/config` — brand and environment placeholder.

## Code

- TypeScript strict. No `any`.
- Import aliases: `src`, `pages`, `containers`, `components`, `store`, `utils`.
- Money on screen is formatted text. Do not use binary floats for amounts when real ledger code is added.
- Mocks that look like trading must say Demo / simulated. Never fake a filled order.
- Original branding only. Do not copy another broker's name, logo, or copy.
- Keep the CFD risk warning visible on public pages.

## Product phase

The React app stays at the repo root. Node and MongoDB start in `BE/`. Do not add Postgres. Keep the API package inside `BE/` so the frontend and backend can deploy separately. Deploys go through GitHub Actions, not Vercel.
